e like ♦7, so I should take control here with a moderate card to keep the flow manageable.  \n\n**Reason:**  \n♦8 is the cheapest win that accomplishes beating the last play without wasting higher cards. It also keeps the pressure low, allowing my teammate to potentially win the next trick with a moderate card if needed. Using ♦8 now preserves ♣2 and RedJoker for bombs or critical singles later, while also forcing the Landlord to use something higher if they want to regain the lead.  \n\n**Answer:**  \n{"cards": ["♦8"]}'}
